{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>They</b> — The masters of the voice of knowledge said that the order of the heavens and their laws will pass away, and HaShem will renew new heavens and a new earth, and they need to interpret the words of Jeremiah, who wrote \"If these laws depart,\" and the words of David: \"and He established them forever and ever; He gave a decree and it shall not pass.\" And Rabbi Judah ben David, the first grammarian who was in the land of the West, said that the universals are preserved forever and the particulars perish. And the correct interpretation: that this earth — it is the dry land."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:53.928788978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}